I replaced the linear scan with a lazily built 65536-entry lookup table, so repeated message lookups become a single indexed load while preserving first-match semantics for duplicate numbers. Building the table once costs only `MESGS` iterations and removes the per-call loop.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```